     "explanation": "Once a growth team locks in an aha moment, the entire activation funnel — onboarding flow, lifecycle emails, in-product nudges, sales targeting — gets reverse-engineered around it. If the aha is wrong (a correlation without causation, a vanity proxy), months of cross-functional work get pointed at the wrong target. The real activation lever stays neglected. This is why Ellis insists on the mechanism check before committing.",
