     "explanation": "Only content marketing meets both of Ellis's heuristic guardrails: LTV/CAC above 3 (4.5) and payback under 12 months (8). The other three channels all violate at least one criterion — Google and LinkedIn fall short of the 3x ratio, and their payback periods exceed the 12-month threshold. Trade shows fail both badly. Scaling them would burn cash. Scaling content is the rational call.",
