     "title": "Practice: Design Your 90-Day Stand-Up",
     "content": "You've been hired as Growth Lead at a product of your choice. Map your **first 90 days** in writing, following the Atlassian template:\n\n**Days 1-30 — Foundation**\n• What 5 hires (or role assignments) do you make?\n• What's your NSM and how do you defend it?\n• What's the first dashboard you build?\n• When and how do you run the Ellis must-have survey?\n\n**Days 31-60 — Diagnose**\n• What 3 analyses do you commission? (cohort, aha, channel CAC)\n• What's your first \"why is this metric flat?\" investigation?\n• When do you first present findings to leadership?\n\n**Days 61-90 — Ship**\n• What are your first 5 ICE-ranked experiments?\n• What weekly cadence do you lock in?\n• What's your post-mortem ritual?\n• What's the metric movement you commit to leadership by Day 90?\n\nDeliverable: a one-page 90-day plan. The exercise of writing it forces you to operationalize every concept from this course. Reread your Lesson 1 mindset audit — notice how your perspective has changed.",
